WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.433
Focus beats idea hopping.

00:00:01.433 --> 00:00:06.090
Fourteen days on one idea teaches more than fourteen ideas in a day.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.314
This lesson is about one idea for 14 days.

00:00:09.314 --> 00:00:11.822
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:15.404
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.404 --> 00:00:20.778
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.778 --> 00:00:24.719
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.719 --> 00:00:29.376
Stay practical: commit to one idea window before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.490
Commit to one idea window.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.360
Write the start date and the kill date.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.230
Remember the objective: commit to one idea window.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:41.177
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.177 --> 00:00:45.482
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:49.428
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.428 --> 00:00:53.734
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:56.245
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.245 --> 00:00:57.680
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.254
During the window: talk to people, ship tiny tests, and do not switch for boredom.

00:01:03.254 --> 00:01:06.056
Remember the objective: commit to one idea window.

00:01:06.056 --> 00:01:09.909
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:14.112
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:14.112 --> 00:01:17.965
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:01:17.965 --> 00:01:22.168
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:01:22.488 --> 00:01:27.100
After fourteen days, keep, kill, or change with evidence - not vibes.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.174
Remember the objective: commit to one idea window.

00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:34.402
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:34.402 --> 00:01:39.013
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:39.013 --> 00:01:43.241
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:01:43.241 --> 00:01:47.853
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:01:47.853 --> 00:01:50.543
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.080
